-- statement:
--   A source-exact Chat 06 consumer on the original spectrally negative Lévy X, original dividend control and original rightCont filtration. It constructs the physical finite-horizon predictable clock and proves the literal inclusive ruin-stopped discounted C² Taylor jump difference is P-integrable and has zero expectation, assuming only the genuine source future marked rectangle intensity and a natural exhausting sequence of finite X.ν negative-mark rate bands. Unlike the previous consumer, no independent hLocal source occupation finiteness is assumed; it follows from the already Proved original initial/future two-sector mass theorem. Infinite first moment of small negative jumps remains allowed; the Taylor O(z²) residual supplies L¹/L².
